       1 = g6m4 prints every fabric's config (one line each, every field) where it would create it, then exits with code
       4 before the first: no file, fabric, network or GPU work. The fabrics the built model completes show what the options set.
       Compares the fabric bring-up of two builds (docs/HOST-CORE.md, R6c).
+  GR8_FABRIC_TC:
+    scope: agree
+    kind: int
+    default: "0"
+    values: "0..255"
+    doc: >-
+      IP traffic class (the whole TOS byte, DSCP << 2 | ECN) that the fabric's RC queue pairs send with. 0 leaves the
+      traffic unmarked, as upstream does, so a switch that classifies by DSCP puts it in its best-effort queue. 106 is
+      DSCP 26 plus ECT(0), the usual lossless-RoCE class. Set it on every rank alike, and only after the NICs
+      (trust dscp, PFC on the matching priority) and the switch (DSCP 26 to a PFC-protected traffic class) are set up for it.
   GR8_GEN_CACHE:
